<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Ghost Ridge from Barlow Pass by the Twin Lakes Trail (PCT)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:174-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.282436" lon="-121.685554"><ele>1267.4</ele><name>Barlow Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:barlow-pass-sno-park (OSM way 129814976); confidence: high; pdf_page: 174; book_elev_ft: 4157; quote: From the northeast corner of Barlow Pass Sno-Park climb the snow bank, go several yards, turn right (south), and ski ... along the Pacific Crest Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.267730" lon="-121.693060"><ele>1387.4</ele><name>High point of the Twin Lakes Trail (PCT), past The Shoulder</name><desc>source: OSM PCT node at the trail's DEM high point (4,552 ft); confidence: high; pdf_page: 174; book_elev_ft: 4550; quote: The trail climbs moderately to The Shoulder and then on to the nearby high point (4,550 feet) 1.3 miles from the trailhead</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.266200" lon="-121.695800"><ele>1429.8</ele><name>Open slope west of the trail</name><desc>source: placed from the text: west of the high point through small trees onto the slope (DEM about 4,650 ft); confidence: low; pdf_page: 176; quote: Leave the trail and enter dense, small trees to the west, quickly reaching an open slope</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.263700" lon="-121.697500"><ele>1471.5</ele><name>Western edge of the slope (lower overlook)</name><desc>source: placed from the text and DEM (about 4,800 ft on the slope's west side); confidence: low; pdf_page: 176; book_elev_ft: 4800; quote: Climb this slope (4,800 feet) to its western edge for the best views</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.262324" lon="-121.696695"><ele>1503.8</ele><name>Ghost Ridge summit</name><desc>source: OSM node 5257209461 'Ghost Ridge' (natural=peak); DEM 4,934 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 160; book_elev_ft: 4925; quote: map 35: GHOST RIDGE 4925'; text: climb moderately through forest ... then the top of Ghost Ridge, which is clear of trees</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Ghost Ridge from Barlow Pass by the Twin Lakes Trail (PCT)</name><desc>1. Barlow Pass Sno-Park -&gt; High point of the Twin Lakes Trail (PCT), past The Shoulder: osm (high), 1.17 mi | 2. High point of the Twin Lakes Trail (PCT), past The Shoulder -&gt; Open slope west of the trail: straight (low), 0.17 mi | 3. Open slope west of the trail -&gt; Western edge of the slope (lower overlook): straight (low), 0.19 mi | 4. Western edge of the slope (lower overlook) -&gt; Ghost Ridge summit: straight (medium), 0.10 mi</desc>
